<span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">difference_type<span class=\"br0\">(</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">get</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>k<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i.<span class=\"me1\">current_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">get</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>k<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>j.<span class=\"me1\">current_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. Returns the smallest absolute value among <code><i>DIST(n)</i></code> for all integers <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">0</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> sizeof...<span class=\"br0\">(</span>Views<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>These functions are not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>zip_view::<i>iterator</i>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> i, j\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the iterators.\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> n\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> position relative to current location.\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1,2)</span> a copy of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">i</span></code> that is advanced by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">n</span></code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> a copy of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">i</span></code> that is advanced by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span>n</span></code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> the distance between <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">i</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">j</span></code></div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/zip_view/iterator/operator_arith\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator++</span><span>operator++<span>(int)</span></span><span>operator--</span><span>operator--<span>(int)</span></span><span>operator+=</span><span>operator-=</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  advances or decrements the underlying iterators <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/zip_view","title":"std::ranges::views::zip, std::ranges::zip_view"},{"path":"ranges/zip_view/iterator","title":"std::ranges::zip_view<Views...>::iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"operator+,-(ranges::zip_view::iterator)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Let current_ denote the underlying tuple-like object of iterators to elements of adapted views."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"i, j, n"},{"label":"Return value","note":"a copy of i that is advanced by n"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator++, operator++(int), operator--, …","note":